I am glad that Paul brought this up, because it does tend to look bad.  I 
have stopped using save files and now only run normal games.  I do tend to
die a lot less, and ghost stacks are harder to come by, but the thrill of
getting on the high score list is much greater.

Actually, this brings up a question?  On my best real game, I was at the
Medusa level, but don't you just hate it when you get here and you have none 
of the useful items needed at your disposal?  All I had was a mirror.  Not 
this would have worked, cause the room she was in had 3 doors, but she kept
moving and the mirror kept getting fogged up or she wouldn't look.  Is this
dependant on distance from her?  I finally die when she left the room, I went
in, chased her to the next room, and she jumped back and got me.  Is there any
way to pin her down and kill from a distance.  I mean I was REALLY devoid of
nice, useful items.

Of course, the REAL 'worst normal game' I had was one in which I had gotten 12
or so wishes, but forgot how much damage hitting an ochre jelly can do.  I
was, ahem, unhappy.


